  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency Movement and Relocation Assistance for Somalia, Eritrean, Sudan and South Sudan Refugees in Somali, Tigray, Afar, Benishangul-Gumuz and Gambella Regions of Ethiopia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ethiopia has a long-standing history of receiving refugees and is currently the third-largest refugee hosting country in Africa and one of the largest refugee asylum countries worldwide, reflecting the ongoing fragility and conflict in the East and Horn of Africa region. Among the principal factors for this are the prevailing political environment in Eritrea, together with the political turmoil, conflict and drought in Sudan, South Sudan and Somalia. Through this project, IOM aims to assist 20,000 refugees from Somalia, Eritrea, Sudan, and South Sudan with timely, safe, and dignified emergency  movement assistance services and relocation assistance from entry points to designated camps, from one camp to another, as well as from conflict-affected camps or temporary conflict induced sites to new and safe locations or camps in Somali, Amhara, Afar, Benishangul Gumuz and Gambella regions of Ethiopia.</narrative>
  </description>
